Atlas overlay patch 0122: fed/fed-glyph
Why: on a fed:// page the security indicator of the location bar is not the padlock but the Federate mark
 (lead, 2026-11-05): a page the helper verified (HTTP status 200) shows the mark, a page whose check failed
 (502, nothing of it shown) shows the dangerous icon, any other answer keeps the engine's icon. The security
 level itself stays NONE (the scheme is secure; there is no "Not secure" chip). One override at the top of
 GetVectorIconOverride(); the choice and the vector icon are new files (chrome/browser/atlas/fed).
Files: chrome/browser/ui/toolbar/chrome_location_bar_model_delegate.cc, chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
Test filter: *AtlasFedLocationIcon*; journey: the omnibox of fed://home.fed shows the mark
Rebase risk: L (one early return in a short function, one dependency line)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, base tree plus the patches before it in the series (dev slot 4)

